Now I have a comprehensive view. Let me identify Round 6 refactoring targets:

1. **`Organism.remove()` and `Organism.removeFromField()` share duplicated cleanup logic** — `remove()` does:
   ```java
   setDead();
   if (location != null) {
       field.clear(location);
       location = null;
       setField(null);
   }
   removed = true;
   ```
   `removeFromField()` does:
   ```java
   if (location != null) {
       field.clear(location);
       location = null;
       field = null;
   }
   ```
   The field-clearing part is the same. `remove()` could call `removeFromField()`:
   ```java
   protected void remove() {
       setDead();
       removeFromField();
       removed = true;
   }
   ```
